WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:08.884
A grading scheme turns marks into grades and decides who passes. You choose a starting template, then adjust it to your school's rules.

00:00:12.952 --> 00:00:15.960
Open Grading in the menu, then click New scheme.

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:31.820
Choose the 9-band scale, CBSE-style. It gives grades A1 to E from percentage bands, with 33 percent to pass each subject. This is a starting template: please check it against your board's current rules.

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:40.906
Give the scheme a clear name, such as Class 10 grading, and click Create scheme.

00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:47.957
Here you see every band and the pass mark. You can change any of them before you use the scheme.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:57.902
The Try it box calculates sample marks with this scheme, so you can check the result before any real examination.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:10.275
Back in the list, the first scheme is already your school's default, so new examinations use it. With more than one scheme, choose Make default from its menu.

00:01:14.511 --> 00:01:22.078
If you change a scheme later, ScoreCode saves a new version. Results that were already processed keep the version they used.

00:01:25.828 --> 00:01:29.679
Next, we add the students of Class 10, Section A.
